  "_note": "backends.<serverInfo.name> is the SEED for that backend: params corrects the derived gene parameters ({\"tool.param\": \"gene\" | null}; every null needs an entry in reasons), forms swaps the probe gene, known_failures lists expected-fail keys \"tool.param:form\". This file is vendored byte-identical and owned by the router. A backend that changes its block (a fix deletes a key) writes the block to tests/conformance/identifiers.local.json, which replaces the seed and survives re-vendoring; the router's seed is then pruned at leisure. Seeded 2026-11-20 from router #343: known_failures from the audit (clinvar, gencc, metadome and mgi name the audited tool with the Ensembl form inferred); params, reasons and forms from the pinned tool schemas, not from a run against those backends.",
